siderations:**\n- Seven Pairs (24 points) is much more valuable than All Pungs (6 points) + Pung of Honors (1 point) = 7 points\n- Peng F3 would expose my hand and eliminate the Seven Pairs possibility\n- With 4 unshown W3, 4 unshown B3, 3 unshown B4, I have reasonable chances to complete Seven Pairs\n\nReason: Passing preserves the opportunity to pursue Seven Pairs (24 points), which is a high-value pattern. Currently I have 5 natural pairs (W1, W3, B4, B8, F3) and a triple F4. By keeping my hand concealed, I can work towards converting the F4 triple into a pair and finding one more pair to complete Seven Pairs. This strategy is more valuable than exposing a F3 pung for minimal points (6-7 points total), which would also destroy my Seven Pairs potential.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
